# Claude Code on local models

One command. It starts a small proxy if needed, then opens Claude Code against oMLX at `http://127.0.0.1:8000`.

oMLX must already be running, and the model must be loaded. Only one big model fits at a time.

```bash
cd ~/Agent_learning && claude-local
```

That uses the default, `qwen-flash`.

## Pick a model

```bash
cd ~/Agent_learning && claude-local qwen-flash
cd ~/Agent_learning && claude-local glm-flash
cd ~/Agent_learning && claude-local qwen-27b
cd ~/Agent_learning && claude-local deepseek
```

| Nickname | Weights in `~/MLX_Models` |
|---|---|
| `qwen-flash` | `Qwen3.8-Flash-Next-MLX-8bit-MTP` |
| `glm-flash` | `GLM-5.3-Flash-MLX-6bit` |
| `qwen-27b` | `Qwen3.8-27B-mxfp8` |
| `deepseek` | `DeepSeek-V4.1-Flash-oQ4e-mtp` |

`deepseek` works only after that download finishes and the model is loaded in oMLX. Unload GLM and Flash-Next first. It needs most of the 512 GB.

Anything after the nickname is passed to Claude Code:

```bash
claude-local qwen-flash -p "hello"
```

## Stop the proxy

```bash
claude-local --stop
```

Do this once after the model list changes (`~/.litellm/local-claude.yaml`), then start `claude-local` again. A proxy that is already running will not see a new nickname.
